{
 "what": "Design-phase simulator pilot of E29, run on 21 November 2026 before the plan of e29_hardware_sqd_active_space.py was written; no device sample existed. N2 in cc-pVDZ, CAS(10 electrons, 12 orbitals), 24 qubits, 627,264 determinants, bond lengths 1.09 and 1.8 Angstrom; 4 groups per bond; a group is 50 circuits of the product's builder (sqdrift.build_sqdrift_circuits, circuits_per_time 25, terms_per_circuit 10, evolution times 1 and 10, seed point_seed(29, 0, bond index, k)) with 100 shots per circuit from the product's simulator call (circuit_runner.run_measured_circuits, Aer, one call per circuit, seed = builder seed + 2113 x circuit index). Arms: N the noiseless samples; NS the same shuffled within each qubit's marginal (generator point_seed(29, 1, bond index, k)); U 5,000 uniform bitstrings (generator point_seed(29, 2, bond index, k)). Every cell is one call of the product's sqdrift.diagonalize(problem, counts, samples_per_batch=S, num_batches=3, max_iterations=5, seed=k), S = 300 (the product's default), 100 and 30. The product's diagonalize did not give the number of bits to BitArray.from_counts then (it does since commit d65eea48); the pilot recorded the width qiskit inferred from the counts of every cell and was written to run a cell with a width below 24 a second time with the width given from outside. Every cell had the width 24, so no cell was run that way and every number here is from the product's call. Produced by the scripts under /tmp/e29dev (e29_problem.py, e29_sample.py, e29_pilot.py); rows are the rows of /tmp/e29dev/pilot_rows.jsonl, one per cell: that file held 90 rows for 72 cells, because 18 cells of arm U were run twice; the two runs have the same energy, dimension and iterations and differ in seconds only; the later row is kept, as the tables take it. error_mha is E - E_FCI in mHa; dimension is the subspace dimension; distinct_valid, valid_fraction and hf_fraction describe the input samples (configurations with 5 alpha and 5 beta electrons; share equal to the Hartree-Fock determinant); tables is the text of /tmp/e29dev/task4_tables.log.",
